  "content": {
    "id": "p10-q23-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Let $T_n$ denote the $n$th triangular number.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p10-q23-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Prove that $8T_n+1$ is a perfect square.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$8T_n+1=(2n+1)^2$.\n\nSubstitute $T_n=\\dfrac{n(n+1)}{2}$ and factorise.",
          "worked": "Using $T_n=\\dfrac{n(n+1)}{2}$,\n$$\\begin{align*}\n8T_n+1&=8\\times\\frac{n(n+1)}{2}+1\\\\\n8T_n+1&=4n(n+1)+1\\\\\n8T_n+1&=4n^2+4n+1\\\\\n8T_n+1&=(2n+1)^2.\n\\end{align*}$$\nSince $2n+1$ is an integer, $8T_n+1$ is a perfect square.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 42
      },
      {
        "id": "p10-q23-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Draw a picture illustrating the identity you found in part (a).",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Eight triangular groups of $T_n$ dots and one central dot form a square with $2n+1$ dots on each side.",
          "worked": "For example, when $n=3$, each triangular group contains $T_3=6$ dots. Eight such groups surround one central dot to form a $7\\times7$ square:\n$$8T_3+1=8\\times6+1=49=7^2.$$\nThe same arrangement for general $n$ gives a square with $2n+1$ dots on each side.",
          "solutionDiagrams": [
            {
              "id": "p10-q23-b-solution-dots",
              "role": "solution",
              "format": "tikz",
              "code": "% mathsmap-diagram-colours {\"version\":1,\"kind\":\"geometry\",\"base\":[],\"semantic\":[{\"name\":\"groupRed\",\"hex\":\"EF6068\",\"reason\":\"distinguishes triangular groups\"},{\"name\":\"groupBlue\",\"hex\":\"268CFF\",\"reason\":\"distinguishes adjacent triangular groups\"},{\"name\":\"centreOrange\",\"hex\":\"EF8B2C\",\"reason\":\"identifies the additional central dot\"}],\"reference\":\"teacher PDF page 80, question 23(b)\"}\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[x=7mm,y=7mm]\n\\special{dvisvgm:raw <metadata data-graph-strokes=\"1\"/>}\n\\definecolor{groupRed}{HTML}{EF6068}\n\\definecolor{groupBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}\n\\definecolor{centreOrange}{HTML}{EF8B2C}\n\\path[use as bounding box] (-0.45,-0.45) rectangle (6.45,6.45);\n\\foreach \\x in {0,...,6}{\\foreach \\y in {0,...,6}{\\fill[groupBlue] (\\x,\\y) circle[radius=2.8mm];}}\n\\foreach \\x/\\y in {0/6,4/6,5/6,6/6,0/5,1/5,4/5,5/5,0/4,1/4,2/4,4/4,2/2,4/2,5/2,6/2,1/1,2/1,5/1,6/1,0/0,1/0,2/0,6/0}{\\fill[groupRed] (\\x,\\y) circle[radius=2.8mm];}\n\\fill[centreOrange] (3,3) circle[radius=2.8mm];\n\\end{tikzpicture}",
              "src": null,
              "widthMm": 60,
              "alt": "Mathematical diagram",
              "overlayOf": null,
              "transparent": false,
              "axes": null,
              "spec": {
